  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A\\subset \\mathbb{N}$ be an infinite set for which there exists some $\\epsilon>0$ such that in any subset of $A$ of size $n$ there is a subset of size at least $\\epsilon n$ which contains no three-term arithmetic progression.\nIs it true that $A$ is the union of a finite number of sets which contain no three-term arithmetic progression?",
